  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "zend_std_write_property",
    "file": "php-src/Zend/zend_object_handlers.c",
    "description": "Use-after-free in typed-property write path: zend_std_write_property caches variable_ptr = OBJ_PROP(zobj, property_offset), then calls zend_verify_property_type() on a temp zval. Type verification may coerce object-to-string via __toString(), which can run user code that overwrites the same variable holding the target object ($a=\"\"), dropping the last ref and freeing zobj. After returning, zend_std_write_property still writes Z_PROP_FLAG_P(variable_ptr)=0 (line ~796) using the stale pointer from the freed object. The missing revalidation/liveness check after re-entrant user code is the root cause.",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires assignment to a typed property where type checking performs coercion that invokes user code (e.g., assigning object to string-typed property, causing __toString()). During __toString(), attacker-controlled code must destroy/overwrite the original object reference (e.g., global $a reassigned), so the object is freed before zend_std_write_property resumes. Execution then continues in the same write_property call and touches cached property storage, causing UAF write."
  },
